            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "id": 103820,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Created attachment 3902\npatch v3: free readLines() buffers with a shared cleanup context\n\nThis patch supersedes attachment 3901. I've deferred R_realloc(): my implementation invalidated allocation-stack marks saved by R_ToplevelExec() and R_UnwindProtect(), making error unwinding unsafe. That needs a separate fix.\n\nThe readLines() patch keeps malloc()/realloc() and uses one cleanup context for the buffer and any connection opened by the reader. Cleanup frees the buffer first, since closing can also raise an error.\n\nRegression tests pass in normal and strict-barrier builds. Leak checks, including read and close failures, report no leaks.\n\nPatch also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/363.",
            "bug_id": 19208,
            "count": 4,
            "creation_time": "2026-10-09T03:26:44Z"
          },
